I've started Nethack long time ago with pencil and paper notes (probably
with similar content as with the #annotate patch), then I switched to
files (which I often forgot to clean up, so I've got confused), and now
I make in-game notes. The reason for the latter is the tight coupling
of information and actual game. I've occasionally interrupted a game for
a couple weeks, or even months. And when I'm restarting the game now I
can reliably inspect a couple of basic information with the necessary
certainty. (It's not that I couldn't do that with an decoupled external
file with sufficient bookkeeping care, just convenience.)

(I'm still using an external file for interesting events/constellations,
which I collect for postings here once in a while. In this case the
correlation and coupling to an actual game is typically unnecessary.)

